A||||11||BBBAD GT||Whats your V8 Fiero MPG?||||5||
Z||000000||BBBAD GT||04-30-2001||11:55 PM||||I just swapped out my old 600 cfm Edelbrock carb for a new one, and went from getting 160 miles from a full tank (10 gal tank), to approx 160 from a 3/4 tank. 160 miles from 8 gallons is 20 mph!!!  <P>I'm curious what other V8 Fieros are getting, and what injection/trans are you running (I got the stock Isuzu 5-speed)?<P><P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero/V8sig.jpg">        <P><A HREF="http://home.att.net/~nomercy5.0/V8Specs.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8 For Sale</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Hartz||05-01-2001||08:25 AM||||Hey there,<P>I've got a mostly stock 350 TPI from an '89 Trans Am GTA  (with headers and a few bolt ons - nothing major) mated to a 5 speed Getrag transmission.  If I keep my foot out of it in highway driving, I can get 20 MPG.  Around town, with more "typical" driving, I get maybe 17-18 MPG.  <P>20 MPG with a carb is awesome.  Great job!<P>Hartz||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfixit58||05-01-2001||09:01 AM||||Interesting... The final gear ratio is the biggest contributor to economy, especially when it comes to highway miles. I installed a 300 HP 350 in my buddy's 68 Camaro along with a 700r4. With the stock 2.97:1 rear end (was a 6 cyl car) we got 24 mpg at 70 mph with a stock QuadraJet. When we changed to a 3.4:1 posi and Holley 650, mileage went to about 18 mpg. It sure makes you wish a 6-speed tranny was available.<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||BBBAD GT||05-01-2001||01:32 PM||||I hear ya Roy, cruising at 65 mph is around 2.2-2.3k rpms, which I would love to bring that down to 1.8-1.9 rpms at 65 mph.  Oh well, can't have it all.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Richard Parnell||05-01-2001||07:24 PM||||I have an Edlebrock 600 carb on my 350 V8 '87 SC and get about 15 mpg.  Not too good but it's just too much fun.  When I open up all four I swear I can see the guage moving.||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroLT1||05-02-2001||07:58 AM||||MPFI (300hp 1995 LT1)<P>normal   (CTY)18   (HWY)25<BR>spirited (CTY)14   (HWY)21<BR>avg.     (CTY)16   (HWY)23<P><P>------------------<BR>Winston Ojeda<BR><B>88 Formula LT1</B><BR>Milwaukee, Wisconsin, USA<BR><A HREF="http://www.FieroLT1.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.FieroLT1.com</A><BR><I>Home of the Fiero LT1</I><BR> <A HREF="mailto:wojeda@FieroLT1.com">wojeda@FieroLT1.com</A> ||||reg||6
Z||000006||Archie||05-04-2001||09:21 PM||||I've just returned from a trip to Pontiac, MI to run the First leg of the Power Tour.<P>Ran from there down to Joliet, IL. with my Finale 270HP LM1 V-8 with TPI. Running speeds in the 70 to 80 range Averaged 26.23 MPG for the trip including 2 drives thru Detroit.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000007||LT1 Chop Top||05-05-2001||05:55 PM||||I got about 25 mpg when I drove the Chop Top from Chicago to Texas, in town about 18-20.||||reg||1
